  "findings": [
    "Current production emits typed aliases; M1 directly emitted expanded coefficient recipes. TraceDefinitions::retain infers each sum and allocates a typed handle, and with_aliases revalidates definitions.",
    "Metric scheduling raises free12 gamma time substantially even when the final free-index trace has no metric contraction to perform.",
    "Axial epsilon scheduling is the largest extra cost. Its registry-wide epsilon flag enters collection for every domain, and collection can open and copy metric-only alias definitions. The shared collection parser still uses depth_limit=None; this is distinct from the shallow contraction planner.",
    "Default axial definition payload grows from 45,606 to 481,987 bytes versus gamma-only while keeping 103 aliases, the same exact materialized answer and the scalar spectator literal. The later broad output stage is dominated by spectator-interface reconstruction (157 ms in a separate CPU 8 split), not alias expansion (21 ms)."
  ],
